WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:03.439
I'm outside the Bank of England

00:00:03.439 --> 00:00:07.619
and under that building is more than a
hundred billion pounds' worth of gold.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.719
But I'm here to talk about

00:00:09.719 --> 00:00:13.320
significantly more sensible amounts of money
specifically banknotes

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:16.940
If you have a look on pretty much any banknote in

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:20.380
pretty much many any major currency in the
world, you'll find little yellow rings.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:24.180
On the back of the British £10 note they are the pollen around the flower

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:27.140
around the flower, next to Charles Darwin.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:31.220
On the US $20 bill, they are the numbers
in the "20"s, in the background.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:34.260
This is called the EURion constellation or at least that's that name it was given

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:37.810
by the German computer scientist called Markus Kuhn

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:41.080
who discovered it. You put this into a colour photocopier

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:42.610
and its image processing algorithms

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:45.020
will recognized this pattern. It's designed to be

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:49.450
really easy for computers to recognize and it will refuse to copy it.

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:53.980
Which means that if you want stop from
copying something, put this image on it.

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:57.130
Of course,  you can still just take a picture of it
and print it out but

00:00:57.130 --> 00:01:00.200
if you are forging bank notes with a colour photocopier

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.640
something has probably gone wrong with your life.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:05.760
And that is something you may not have known.

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:09.240
